  441: 
  442: ## Proportionality and gates
  443: 
  444: **This item is SLICED. The code gate runs twice, once per slice.** The reason is size measured
  445: rather than felt: five acceptance ids, ten test bodies, a new shipped module, a migration carrying
  446: the tree's first policy set, three edge functions, two adapters and two conformance arms. One diff
  447: review over all of that would return a wall of findings in which the important ones are
  448: indistinguishable from the rest. The slice boundary is the item boundary - slice 1 is AI4DEV-66's
  449: two denial ids, slice 2 is AI4DEV-67's three grant ids - so each slice is also a complete,
  450: reviewable claim.
  451: 
  452: The policy set lands whole in slice 1 (step 5) even though slice 2's positives read it, because a
  453: policy set is one object and splitting it would make slice 1's denials vacuous.
  454: 
  455: ## Rides along
  456: 
  457: Nothing yet. Machinery changed while working this item is listed here and in the pull request.
