  157: /**
  158:  * An authenticated session, and WHICH PROVIDER ESTABLISHED IT.
  159:  *
  160:  * `provider` is recorded, never simulated. Supabase Auth records the provider that produced a
  161:  * session; how the session was obtained â€” an email and a password, or a completed Google consent
  162:  * round trip â€” happens entirely upstream of anything this requirement's leaf ships. AT-001.03's
  163:  * body asserts that `completeSignup` behaves identically for `'google'` and `'email'`, which is a
  164:  * real property of the shipped decision module (it never reads this field). It is NOT a claim that a
  165:  * Google round trip works: see the suite's own note on AT-001.03, and the plan's per-id table.
  166:  *
  167:  * `'github'` joins the two for AT-001.02 and carries exactly the same caveat: a github-established
  168:  * session is the state Auth is in AFTER a consent round trip, and no handshake is simulated to reach
  169:  * it. The establishing provider still participates in NO decision the shipped modules make â€” the
  170:  * volunteer gate reads a LINKED IDENTITY, which is a different fact (see `linkGithubIdentity`).
  171:  */
  172: export type SessionProvider = 'email' | 'google' | 'github';
