  207: // `edge.ts`, so a loop-tier green over an expired or revoked session grades byte for byte the code
  208: // both deployed functions run on every authenticated request. This file decides WHICH sessions are
  209: // live, which is vendor bookkeeping; it never decides what a dead answer means.
  210: import { callerFromAuthAnswer, type Caller } from '../../../../supabase/functions/_shared/caller.ts';
  211: // THE SHIPPED PER-ORGANISATION ROLE JUDGEMENT â€” the ONE thing that decides whether an admin-only
  212: // NGO-side action is permitted in the target organisation. `update-organization` imports the same
  213: // function, so a loop-tier green over AT-001.16 and AT-001.36 grades the code that ships. This file
  214: // supplies the membership ROW it judges, which is storage; it never decides what a role means.
  215: import { orgAdminActionAllowed } from '../../../../supabase/functions/_shared/memberships.ts';
  216: // THE SHIPPED IMPORT STUB. The IMPORT SOURCE is the shipped stub, not a copy living in this file â€”
  217: // AT-001.05 compares the profile it reads back against `stubGithubStatsFor`, so if the two were
  218: // separate implementations the test would grade the fixture's copy and say nothing about what the
  219: // edge function writes.
  220: //
  221: // `extractGithubHandle` USED TO BE IMPORTED HERE TOO and is not any more, and that is a narrowing
  222: // rather than a loss. It is still on the tested path â€” `callerFromAuthAnswer` calls it, on the
